{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789314344,"nonce":"3V/KBhBWcTxsZMtvaFuoPhHGRYg=","title":"Inliner: admit callees that call, at hot sites, and keep error paths cold","message":"The inliner refused any callee containing a call. Every library helper on a hot path has one (`zb_list_get_ptr` has a bounds check that raises, `zb_math_sqrt` a domain check), so in a Python loop over a list every element access and every sqrt stayed a call, and the guards with them. The typed nbody port ran 2.5x slower than the ZynML @reference port on the same algorithm.\n\nChanges in `inline.rs`:\n\n- A callee whose calls are all direct (`Function`, `Symbol`, `FuncRef`) is admitted, under a tighter size cap (`MAX_INLINE_INSTS_WITH_CALLS`), and only at sites inside a loop of the caller (`blocks_in_loops`). Elsewhere the call costs less than the code it would bring.\n- Callers and callees in one strongly connected component of the direct call graph (`call_cycles`, Tarjan) are never inlined into each other. Without this `zb_any_repr` / `zb_seq_repr_any` / `zb_list_items_any` grew into each other round after round until the caller budget stopped them, at the size of the budget, and a trivial program's compile went from under half a second to over two.\n- A caller past `MAX_POST_INLINE_INSTS_WITH_CALLS` takes no more call-bearing callees.\n- A callee with `attributes.cold`, `no_inline` or `InlineHint::Never` is refused. `@cold` and `@noinline` annotations set these in lowering; the builtins DSL has `define_cold` (used for `zb_fatal`) and the Python frontend marks `zb_hook_raise` cold.\n- Nothing is inlined at a site from which every path calls a cold function (`blocks_leading_to_cold`, a greatest fixpoint over the CFG). An error's message is built before the cold call that reports it, and inlining `zb_any_str` / `zb_any_repr` / `zb_str_repr` there put a `__main__` with one dict lookup in a loop at 379 blocks and 267 ms of codegen; with cold sites excluded it is 16 ms.\n- `blocks_in_loops` walks each back edge with its own visited set, so a block shared with an inner loop no longer stops the outer loop's walk.\n\n`ZYNTAX_TRACE_INLINE=1` names every inline made with its site's hotness. `ZYNTAX_TRACE_OPT_PHASES=1` prints per-pass times per round and the total optimization and codegen time in the tiered runtime.\n\nTyped nbody (Python, `list[Body]`) after: 10M steps in about 0.85 s, ZynML nbody_ref 0.57 s, CPython 45 s. ZynML nbody and nbody_ref unchanged within noise, interleaved A/B against HEAD.\n\nNot done: a callee's size still counts its cold blocks; a function all of whose paths end in a cold call is not itself treated as cold.","files":null}]}